  "id": "nadagam_sinhala",
  "name": "Nadagam (Sinhala folk-drama song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Sung folk drama of Sri Lanka's western coastal belt, adapted in the nineteenth century from South Indian Tamil nadagam and associated with the Catholic communities around Negombo and Moratuwa; Philippu Sinno is remembered as its pioneer. A narrator-singer, the pothe gura, introduces the action and the actors sing their roles to drum and cymbal accompaniment. Ediriweera Sarachchandra drew on it for his stage play Maname. A generic membrane-drum card stands in for the drum and the manjira card for the talampata cymbals.",
  "recipe": "classic modern nadagam, ballad Poetry, indian bard branch. live take. membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, manjira. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
